  "corePolicy": "M01 owns packages/core under Architecture V2. Brush Foundation input, prediction, stabilization, forced-fade and stroke semantics remain frozen. Renderer presentation is transparent/premultiplied: artwork alpha stays in the GPU presentation result and the editor Canvas View owns the white paper/background appearance. Do not bake a white paper into Brush Renderer output. The Android M02 opaque-paper workaround is superseded by this presentation contract. M03 History is Document-owned. Recent Stroke Undo/Redo may use a strictly bounded 16 MiB GPU hot tile cache for one-frame-class response. Cache memory never grows beyond the fixed budget; evicted/oversized history falls back to rebuilding only affected 128px runtime tiles from active formal StrokeRecords. Fallback rebuild presentation is atomic: the old completed canvas remains visible until the rebuilt dirty tiles are complete, then the result is presented once. Full-canvas readback, visible stroke-by-stroke replay, unbounded GPU history, and rebuilding unrelated tiles are forbidden. UI Workspace visibility changes must not invoke Renderer work."
}
